This repository contains no model weights, no container images and no datasets. It contains scripts, patches and
documentation that build and run third-party software. Third-party material and its terms:

Model: deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 at revision 1bae0e1088993b9b82de08f59de5be5a34e42170 (MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek, as in the LICENSE file of the model repository). Download it yourself and follow the terms
  on its model card.

Model overlay: drowzeys/keys-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-Abliterated at revision de412d2249632903dace23399526e00a145aada5,
  file wo_b_l10_35_1017.safetensors (sha256 88324ceaa2c0754a2bdb4ef6bb388a088438e352358343e6c2c882009cdde864). MIT License,
  as stated on its model card. The repository is gated (automatic approval): you must accept its terms on Hugging Face
  before you can download it. Its RESPONSIBLE_USE.md lists prohibited uses, and states that any use prohibited by the
  upstream DeepSeek license is not allowed. The overlay replaces the attn.wo_b weights and scales of layers 10-35 of the
  official checkpoint (26 weights and 26 scales; it removes the model's refusal behaviour). tools/build_overlay_variant.py
  merges it into a copy of the checkpoint on your machine; this repository ships neither the overlay nor a merged
  checkpoint.

vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM project.
  The runtime patches in patches/ modify vLLM source files inside the container at start-up and install modules into the vllm
  package (among them one that runs on vLLM's NCCL wrapper, patches/files/gb10_oneshot_ar.py, and a native NVMe reader for the
  Engram tables, patches/files/engram_nvme/). image/dsv41_bake.py carries the change of vLLM pull request #60762 (kernel block
  sizes on SM12x) to two vLLM source files in the base image at build time.

FlashInfer (https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer), Apache License 2.0, and NVIDIA NCCL
  (https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl, source under the BSD 3-Clause License) are part of the vLLM image. This recipe does not
  modify NCCL. It edits files of FlashInfer's experimental b12x package inside the container at start-up (patches 036 and 037;
  the image on disk is not changed), and patches/files/gb10_twoshot.py, gb10_twoshot_cute.py and gb10_twoshot_proxy.c are derived
  from FlashInfer's b12x RoCE runtime (roce_oneshot.py, _oneshot_cute.py and _roce_proxy.c, Apache License 2.0); patch 018 also calls that runtime
  directly.

vLLM container image (vllm/vllm-openai), used as the base image by digest. It includes NVIDIA CUDA components, among them
  the NCCL binaries, that are distributed under NVIDIA's own license terms.

Benchmark data, downloaded from Hugging Face by the bench/data/ scripts and not redistributed here (check each
  dataset card for the current terms): allenai/WildChat-4.8M (ODC-BY; only user turns are used),
  nebius/SWE-rebench-openhands-trajectories (CC-BY-4.0), zai-org/LongBench-v2 (Apache-2.0) and
  princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Lite_bm25_27K (see its dataset card). The tokenizer files the data scripts need for this
  model come from deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek).
